[Music]  this is joanna she thinks she has  covid19  and now she has a nostril so we can test  her  but this isn't just any nose swab it's  part of a high-tech pcr-like test called  the q-health monitoring system and you  can do it all at home no standing in  line at the testing center and then  waiting a few days to get the result see  first you insert this cartridge into  this cartridge reader then after you've  snotted up this fancy swab it gets  inserted into the cartridge  which then sends the result to your  phone  and confirmed  positive definitely did not want to be  in the same room as her but i am the  real joanna and i recently did have  kovit and i really have been testing two  new advanced at-home molecular tests  on myself  number one the q reader and q covid19  test which together start at 474  number two the detect covid test the  starter kit starts at 75  clearly these are not your 20 something  a pair box of at-home rapid antigen  tests  instead these are at-home molecular  tests that work like pcr tests so do you  really need one of these and if you do  which one do you get we're gonna get to  all of that but first you really need to  understand the difference between these  tests and those inexpensive tests  don't worry she's gonna help with it all  she's far more capable than me  okay first the at-home antigen tests  like these which have been available and  at times hard to find over the past few  months  swab the nose then place six drops here  and then stick the swab in here  here's what's happening those drops of  liquid help push the sample to the paper  and the paper itself is loaded up with  antibodies that detect an antigen or a  viral protein if detected it will be  positive if not negative these tests  which take up to 15 minutes to return  results may not detect covid19 in the  early stages of infection but they tend  to detect it when you're carrying a lot  of the virus on the other hand a  molecular test is more sensitive and can  detect covit earlier these tests use  chemicals and equipment to amplify a  sample's genetic material billions of  times to spot traces of the virus and  now you can do that all from your home  let's try the detect system to  illustrate what's happening during a  molecular test and back to swabbing  after that you insert the swab into this  test tube and stir for 15 seconds  then you open this pouch and get out  this cap and screw it on the tube the  cap has a little enzyme that helps with  the process of amplifying your sample  you shake it up real well so it all gets  mixed up together then you place it in  the detect hub  for about 55 minutes the detect app  which thankfully provides a step-by-step  guide to all this will alert you when  it's ready to be taken out  oh and we're not done then you open  another pack and squeeze the liquid from  this dropper into this reader then you  place your test tube in the chimney of  the reader then finally the sample pours  into the reader then you wait another 10  minutes and then  finally one line negative two lines  positive  the q test does pretty much the same  thing without you having to pretend  you're some sort of mad scientist  you put the q cartridge into the reader  then you put the fancy swab in your nose  and collect the sample  then you insert the swab into the  cartridge  inside it mixes with liquid and some  enzymes and then it does its thing for  about 20 minutes the reader also  connects to your phone via bluetooth  when the test is done boom your results  pop up right in the q health app so  molecular tests can detect your covet  infection earlier than antigen tests but  how much earlier  experts told me it could be anywhere  from six hours to two days and it  depends on a couple of factors including  the variant and that's pretty much how  it went for me on friday i started to  feel symptoms  a rapid antigen test said negative the  detect test positive a pcr test taken  the next morning at a lab confirmed  positive as well  by sunday the rapid antigen test said  positive  both detect and q report that they are  around 97 as accurate as a laboratory  pcr test i called up dr michael minna an  epidemiologist and covid testing expert  to ask him more about these tests and if  we can trust them he previously served  as an advisor to detect yeah you can  certainly trust trust the readout the  tools are working very well uh it's not  a new technology it's just a new  packaging  of a known technology and it's really  sort of taking what only lived in big  instruments and putting it into very  simple little boxes  so which one is better well i love the  queue it's basically a little coved  testing computer but it also costs as  much as a computer the reader is  249. and a pack of three tests is 225  you can buy it on qhealth.com the nba  mlb netflix and google are just a few  using the system eventually q wants to  sell other types of tests including flu  that you'd take and then plug into the  cartridge reader while the detect  requires more steps and takes longer to  process the result it's more affordable  which is why i bought it the starter kit  is 75 and includes the hub and one test  extra tests cost  but the company plans to bring that  price down soon you can buy it on  detect.com if they have stock the site  often says exactly what day and time  there will be more stock in but supplies  go very quickly  detect is also working on a future test  that will test for covid and flu there's  another 75 molecular test called the  lucera check it but it is a single use  test and i didn't try it while i had  kovid and it's really those higher  prices that hold back these tests from  being as useful as the antigen tests  experts told me plus you're going to  want those antigen tests as the virus  progresses and you want to get out of  quarantine  if you're trying to use a test to ask  the question  can i exit isolation and go back to work  or be around my family safely  a rapid antigen test is the test to use  that will give you that information we  just got the results we're both covered  free  molecular tests are so sensitive they  can show positive results even after the  virus is no longer alive in your body  but hey the idea of having a gadget in  your house that saves you a trip to the  doctor is the dream for now though you  need to be willing to pay way more than  those antigen tests luckily fiberglass  joanna is super duper rich  oops

